Statement of Purpose
The law(s) of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) upon the creator(s) and subsequent owner(s) (each and all, an "owner") of an original work of authorship and,or a database (each, a "Work"). 
Certain Owners opt to relinquish those rights to a Work for the purpose of contributing to the public domain, cultural and scientific Work(s) that the public can reliably and without fear of later claims of infringement build upon, modify, incorporate in other Work(s), reuse and redistribute as freely as possible. These Owners may contribute to the public domain to promote the ideal of a free culture and the further production of creative, cultural and scientific Work(s), or to gain reputation or greater distribution for their Work(s) in part through the use and efforts of Other(s).
However, certain Owners might opt to earn compensation including but not limited  to royalties or a licensing fee. Unlike CC0, this License 'The Sovereign License' does not waive commercial right(s). Non-commercial right(s) are granted royalty-free, while commercial right(s) remain subject to licensing agreement(s).

Preamble (This Preamble is for explanatory purpose only and does not create enforceable obligation(s))
This license governs the use and distribution of the Work(s). It grants broad permission(s) for non-commercial use, but explicitly reserves commercial right(s) and requires a separate royalty agreement for any commercial application. The intent is to foster community collaboration while protecting the Owner's commercial interest(s).  This license is designed to allow broad sharing, modification, and redistribution of Work(s), while preserving attribution to the original Author(s) (Licensor). It grants royalty-free right(s) for non-commercial use and mandates royalties for commercial use.

Definitions
"Work(s)": refers to the written material(s), text(s), diagram(s), illustration(s), design(s), specification(s), and,or other creative Work(s) contained in this repository and any subsequent modification(s) or derivative Work(s) created under the terms of this license.
"You or Licensee": refers to any individual, group, or organization accessing, using, or redistributing the Work(s).
"Non-Commercial Use": means any use of the Work(s) for educational, research, personal, charitable or informational purposes, where no direct or indirect monetary compensation, commercial advantage, or financial gain is intended or realized including but not limited to through advertising, sponsorship, or data monetization.
"Commercial Use": Any use of the Work(s) intended for, or directed toward, commercial advantage, profit, sponsorship or monetary compensation, whether direct or indirect including but not limited to advertising, selling, licensing, or integrating the Work(s) into a revenue-generating product or service.
"Author(s)or Owner(s)": The original creator(s) (licensor(s)) of the Work(s).
Contributor(s): Any individual or organization who submit modification(s), addition(s), or improvement(s) to the Work(s).
Performer(s)": refers to any individual(s) who perform, recite, narrate, sing, act, or otherwise contribute live or recorded performances embodied in the Work(s), including but not limited to dramatic, literary, musical, or audiovisual expressions, whether captured in audio, video, or multimedia format.
Derivative Work(s): Any adaptation, translation, transformation, modification, or other work based upon the original Work(s).

